he race stays in Likely Republican territory with wide uncertainty.", "watch": "Early general-election polling or a decisive national shift against the Republican nominee would be the first signs the margin is narrowing.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Montana remains one of the most Republican-leaning states in presidential elections, and the fundamentals point firmly that way again. The state's partisan lean sits at roughly ten points in the Republican column, and no general-election polls or expert ratings have yet been published to test that assumption. With the incumbent president term-limited, both parties will nominate new standard-bearers, removing any incumbency advantage from either side.\n\nThe rating therefore rests on fundamentals alone, and it carries wide uncertainty. Montana's presidential voting pattern has been consistent across recent cycles, and Republicans start with a clear edge. Still, a national environment that turns sharply against the Republican Party, or a Democratic nominee who overperforms in rural states, could narrow the margin. For now the race sits in Likely Republican territory, with the Democratic path to victory requiring a substantial national shift.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1274, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.185, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1774, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1746, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1726, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1793, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.181, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1781, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.172, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "